<title>USA: Illinois 930 MW unit restart still unclear.</title>
<headline>Illinois 930 MW unit restart still unclear.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Illinois Power Co has not yet set a date for a resumption of power production from its 930 megawatt Clinton nuclear power plant, company spokesman John Dewey said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not have a tentative startup date,&quot; Dewey said.</p>
<p>The unit was shut Sept 6 for an originally estimated 70 days of scheduled maintenance and refueling.</p>
<p>&quot;We have to finish our startup readiness action plan and then prove it is effective,&quot; the spokesman said of the continued shutdown.</p>
<p>Illinois Power is a subsidiary Illinova Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk 212 859 1627))</p>
